<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Ukraine says Starlink restricted operations overnight, disrupting military missions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b488f6ef0d4f09e558ebfd9e035faebd22f60beb4d442d0c050997be5295ae75</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T09:14:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-ukraine-says-starlink-restricted-operations-overnight-disrupting-military-missions" /><summary type="html">Elon Musk's Starlink imposed restrictions on the operation of internet terminals in Ukraine overnight, disrupting military missions, an adviser to the Ukrainian president said on Wednesday. The official said Ukraine was given no prior warning about the restrictions to the satellite system it relies on for battlefield operations.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says 'massive' oil, gas and mineral exploration to begin in Greenland</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b913f2686816596d1fb34034f1c6d382f49e71144295856adfde01399b954b4</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T06:41:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-trump-says-massive-oil-gas-and-mineral-exploration-to-begin-in-greenland" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said on Wednesday that a "massive" oil, gas and mineral exploration was slated to begin in Greenland. The US, Denmark and Greenland last month signed a security agreement after Trump's repeated threats to seize control of the island.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine live: Russian drone strike kills six as Ukraine accuses US of helping Putin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b71ba6dd40b2822730fd1a480d201c8cf51b923145b965f22e40c12a49207b1e</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T06:19:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-live-ukraine-massive-russian-attack-on-energy-facilities-at-least-six-dead" /><summary type="html">A Russian drone attack on the western Ukrainian city of Lutsk on Wednesday killed six people and wounded 12, the Ukrainian interior ministry said. Earlier, a senior Ukrainian official accused the United States of helping Russia, saying Washington failed to warn it of incoming strikes and slowed the Starlink system Kyiv relies on for communications and logistics. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>What we know about Pope Leo XIV's lung cancer diagnosis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9b8e2f99cf424ffc4991e33b2aabb91ed77a7eff6fad3453a3209027a7a47a9</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T03:35:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-what-we-know-about-pope-leo-xiv-s-lung-cancer-operation" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo underwent surgery on Tuesday to remove a cancerous tumour from his right lung after saying that a nodule had been "detected at a very early stage". Following a "successful" operation, the Vatican said the 71-year-old pontiff would undergo additional testing.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Kyiv power plant hit by Russian missile without warning from allies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e520d5a788e53b051b8a731f1c6ec6c418d72bf82c8279fc13130f863fa1ee56</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T00:41:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-kyiv-power-plant-hit-by-russian-missile-without-warning-from-allies" /><summary type="html">Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky said Tuesday that a Russian ballistic missile struck a Kyiv power plant without advance warning from Western allies, killing at least two people and wounding around 20. The attack came days after US President Donald Trump announced an energy ceasefire between Moscow and Kyiv, raising questions over efforts to halt strikes on critical infrastructure.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo has cancerous growth removed in lung operation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ba6162f9968789111b9fa3c2d9907d300361f0b9c2cf625df96129b72153edf</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T21:23:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/pope-leo-has-cancerous-growth-removed-in-lung-operation" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV had a cancerous growth removed from his right lung in a 90-minute operation on Tuesday and "woke up normally" after the procedure, the Vatican said. A Vatican source said further tests were being carried out to determine if the cancer had spread. "To ensure the procedure was radical, the lower lobe of the right lung was removed," the Vatican said in a statement. FRANCE 24's Seema Gupta reports from Rome.</summary></entry><entry><title>Have Ukrainian strikes on Yandex data centres hit Russian online disinformation?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a8bf627548259be073737a07e952d1df8094ac557065245e3eaa832d697667d2</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T20:59:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261013-have-ukrainian-strikes-on-yandex-data-centres-hit-russian-online-disinformation" /><summary type="html">After recent Ukrainian bombings of Russian data centres belonging to Yandex, internet users claim to have noticed a sharp reduction in pro-Russian and far-right populist social media content. They suggest the reduction is a direct result of the strikes cutting off Russian disinformation "bots". We examine the claim in this edition of Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Ceuta an 'inalienable' part of Spain, king says on key visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1cd2a6ed810def17d8d40c0f67fbefd5f627f48bf20c582b09398eac8a1007f6</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T19:06:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ceuta-an-inalienable-part-of-spain-king-says-on-key-visit--84d6778d9333.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ceuta-an-inalienable-part-of-spain-king-says-on-key-visit" /><summary type="html">King Felipe VI on Tuesday said Ceuta and Melilla were "an inalienable part" of Spain as he made a landmark visit to the north African territories claimed by neighbouring Morocco. "Ceuta and Melilla are an inalienable part of the political and national reality that is Spain. The sovereignty and territorial integrity of our country are not negotiable," Felipe said. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid.</summary></entry><entry><title>King Felipe VI says Ceuta is ‘inalienable’ part of Spain in landmark visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48b9ae16750b28946e2d1380c6e68ed1b08b8de196cf56318cf52baca041d0f2</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T15:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-spanish-royals-visit-ceuta-amid-tensions-with-morocco-over-migrant-influx--f9df8bcf336a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-spanish-royals-visit-ceuta-amid-tensions-with-morocco-over-migrant-influx" /><summary type="html">King Felipe VI and Queen Letizia visited Ceuta on Tuesday for the first time in 14 years, with the monarch reaffirming Spain’s sovereignty over the North African enclaves claimed by Morocco. The landmark visit comes amid strained relations with Rabat and the aftermath of a mass migrant influx that saw makeshift camps cleared ahead of the royals’ arrival.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Belgium: Greener schools thanks to European funding</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:696200fa801cbbdd6a99ed659aef3c1a6fba5c919d26f5bb5861379d023299b0</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T14:27:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/belgium-greener-schools-thanks-to-european-funding--c7570949caa0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/belgium-greener-schools-thanks-to-european-funding" /><summary type="html">🇧🇪 In Ganshoren, in Belgium, a new school replaces run-down buildings. But the need for renovations remains enormous.👉🏻 Find the whole reporting on France 24 English.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia pounds Ukrainian cities, spares energy targets for first time since Trump 'ceasefire'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d9f534686a98ce0cf755b507ec961cb92df37386dc141b4175373b44bc26dc6</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T13:39:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-russia-pounds-ukrainian-cities-spares-energy-targets-for-first-time-since-trump-ceasefire--9892d97dd176.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-russia-pounds-ukrainian-cities-spares-energy-targets-for-first-time-since-trump-ceasefire" /><summary type="html">Russia hammered Ukrainian cities and transport links overnight into Tuesday, killing at least four people in the city of Kharkiv, while appearing to spare energy facilities for the first time since US President Donald Trump announced an "energy ceasefire" at the weekend. It was not clear whether Moscow had deliberately avoided targeting power plants.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Spanish royals visit crisis-hit Ceuta amid diplomatic tensions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8dc04b9ddc4589ff05aea4e5fb71cb609d4af5921ee8b141eeac7161622669ae</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T13:30:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spanish-royals-visit-crisis-hit-ceuta-amid-diplomatic-tensions--bc891a439a35.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spanish-royals-visit-crisis-hit-ceuta-amid-diplomatic-tensions" /><summary type="html">Spain’s King Felipe VI and Queen Letizia visited Ceuta for the first time since 2007, amid tensions with Morocco following July’s migration crisis, when more than 70,000 people crossed into the Spanish enclave. Most returned to Morocco, but thousands remained, and dozens died. Morocco claims sovereignty over Ceuta, making the royal visit diplomatically sensitive. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris has more from Madrid.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Transactional diplomacy': Greece positioning itself as Trump's most 'reliable ally in the region'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d481c7ac896035eea8a74fa1e9c073da2ca32e5cefab4ef9cfd4583e51c65749</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T11:41:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261013-transactional-diplomacy-greece-positioning-itself-as-the-us-most-reliable-ally-in-the-regio--4880927fce4d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261013-transactional-diplomacy-greece-positioning-itself-as-the-us-most-reliable-ally-in-the-region" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Petros Konstantinidis, a financial journalist for Greece's leading daily newspaper TA NEA. The current controversy surrounding the US ambassador to Greece, Kimberly Guilfoyle, has all the makings of a reality TV show or a telenovela, or both. "This is diplomacy under Trump turning into lifestyle diplomacy," Konstantinidis explains.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Spain’s king visits Ceuta amid tensions with Morocco</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:286373f71a5a6ee5d34f596f3341ae8395449ac297416fdb96fbba6815576e71</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T09:22:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spain-s-king-visits-ceuta-amid-tensions-with-morocco--a4c4f2800cac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spain-s-king-visits-ceuta-amid-tensions-with-morocco" /><summary type="html">King Felipe VI and Queen Letizia are visiting Ceuta months after more than 70,000 migrants arrived from Morocco. While most have returned, thousands remain. The visit has divided residents and risks reigniting diplomatic tensions with Morocco, which claims sovereignty over Ceuta and Melilla.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo XIV admitted to hospital for lung surgery</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:83c27886707e986990f870e29608c2071c5ea4c7f4b5faa6be3847e74d66a13e</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T09:20:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/pope-leo-xiv-admitted-to-hospital-for-lung-surgery--7eb0dd11a883.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/pope-leo-xiv-admitted-to-hospital-for-lung-surgery" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV has been admitted to Rome’s Gemelli hospital for surgery to remove a small lung nodule discovered during recent medical checks. The 71-year-old pontiff said the growth was detected at an early stage. The procedure marks his first hospitalisation since becoming pope in May 2025. FRANCE 24's Seema Gupta has the latest from Rome.</summary></entry><entry><title>French students ‘not giving up the fight’ as 480,000 join new day of school protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1b2329afc76ccba445800d77ef4922ce410ccdac3645cb39ba23d5362d8b02db</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T06:44:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-live-france-braces-for-fresh-nationwide-protests-over-school-conditions--ed166873d347.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-live-france-braces-for-fresh-nationwide-protests-over-school-conditions" /><summary type="html">French students staged another day of nationwide protests on Tuesday over poor school conditions, including teacher shortages and dilapidated buildings, vowing to keep up the pressure ahead of half-term holidays. Around 480,000 protesters joined in on the demonstrations, with Swedish activist Greta Thunberg turning up in Paris to boost the movement’s visibility. Read our liveblog to see how all the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'A positive step': Hungary removes anti-LGBTQ provisions from Orban-era law</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35cc489bdbfa7212412562e30f03d633935f7c6b56baaa493d0367529521d0b5</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T05:15:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-a-positive-step-hungary-removes-anti-lgbtq-provisions-from-orban-era-law--b96f27471fa6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-a-positive-step-hungary-removes-anti-lgbtq-provisions-from-orban-era-law" /><summary type="html">Hungary's parliament voted on Tuesday to remove anti-LGBTQ provisions from a "child protection" law adopted in 2021 under the country's former nationalist leader, in the first significant move to reverse discriminatory legislation since Prime Minister Peter Magyar took power in May.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russia says Europe bought $320 billion in hydrocarbons since 2022</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:206184a7491df0dee6680db51fab9c1feb2f86c0c6d36979a75791da4f7c9dc9</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-13T03:10:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-russia-says-europe-bought-320-billion-in-hydrocarbons-since-2022--d9b66d1b054f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-russia-says-europe-bought-320-billion-in-hydrocarbons-since-2022" /><summary type="html">Russia said on Monday that European Union countries had bought $320.7 billion worth of its energy resources since 2022, despite sanctions over the war in Ukraine. The figure fuelled tensions as European officials criticised a US deal to import Russian diesel, while Stockholm called for the bloc to use frozen Russian assets to boost support for Kyiv.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo diagnosed with lung cancer after doctors successfully remove nodule</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c42e19eb0ef8b76e69724141aab51d459427b0c2804c371ce459b5202e598646</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T22:20:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-what-we-know-about-pope-leo-xiv-planned-lung-operation-this-week--42462f7a7f54.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-what-we-know-about-pope-leo-xiv-planned-lung-operation-this-week" /><summary type="html">Pope ​Leo had a lower lobe ​of his right lung removed during surgery on Tuesday ​and ‌was diagnosed with lung ⁠adenocarcinoma, a common form of ‌lung cancer, the Vatican said in ⁠a medical bulletin. The surgery was successful and the pope is expected to spend a week in hospital recovering. The 71-year-old pontiff is due to travel to Uruguay, Argentina and Peru on November 6, though the Vatican has not confirmed the operation date.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'It's clear that Moscow is just playing with Washington,' analyst says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20c9001ae0929e85d58a22e41c36ffee74d80b231a27bdda28530bdfc72442f5</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T21:02:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261012-it-s-clear-that-moscow-is-just-playing-with-washington-analyst-says--21ae94136adb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261012-it-s-clear-that-moscow-is-just-playing-with-washington-analyst-says" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump's envoys told ​Ukrainian officials on Friday that a deal to allow Russian diesel exports is part of a bid to draw Russia back to negotiations after the failure of previous efforts to launch sustained talks to end the war, three people familiar with the meeting told Reuters. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Grégoire Roos, director of the Europe and Russia and Eurasia Programmes at Chatham House. He says that "it's clear that Moscow is just playing with Washington because Vladimir Putin knows that Donald Trump lives on borrowed time".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>'It's clear that Moscow is just playing with Washington,' analyst says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:730b57478246ec36bf78e4a3ddc9cd1f56e618fe20f40a46478cc27366ee0011</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T20:58:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/it-s-clear-that-moscow-is-just-playing-with-washington-analyst-says--518f477114b7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/it-s-clear-that-moscow-is-just-playing-with-washington-analyst-says" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump's envoys told ​Ukrainian officials on Friday that a deal to allow Russian diesel exports is part of a bid to draw Russia back to negotiations after the failure of previous efforts to launch sustained talks to end the war, three people familiar with the meeting told Reuters. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Grégoire Roos, director of the Europe and Russia and Eurasia Programmes at Chatham House. He says that "it's clear that Moscow is just playing with Washington because Vladimir Putin knows that Donald Trump lives on borrowed time".</summary></entry><entry><title>Tehran denies involvement in UK Fairford air base incident as Britain summons Iranian ambassador</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce70e601ddc7662c79149afdde9904b8d9d1168993746293517781eec9f53e45</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T20:23:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-tehran-denies-involvement-in-uk-fairford-air-base-incident-as-britain-summons-iranian-ambas--9897b235b090.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-tehran-denies-involvement-in-uk-fairford-air-base-incident-as-britain-summons-iranian-ambassador" /><summary type="html">British Prime Minister Andy Burnham on Monday accused Iran's Revolutionary Guards of being responsible for a terror-related incident in September at England's Fairford air base, which is used by the United States military. Following Tehran's denial, the British Foreign Office summoned Iran's Ambassador for talks.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Increasingly evident' Russia won't accept 'energy ceasefire': Zelensky</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f342a113c09d0988136ee6d129806b2dd577fed6f5af006be2c367281ec6c556</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T19:40:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/increasingly-evident-russia-won-t-accept-energy-ceasefire-zelensky--a30b59924184.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/increasingly-evident-russia-won-t-accept-energy-ceasefire-zelensky" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said Monday it was clear that Russia would not agree to stop hitting energy targets, after US President Donald Trump unilaterally announced a deal between the warring nations. "It is increasingly evident that Russia is unwilling to accept an energy ceasefire proposed by the United States," Zelensky said on social media. FRANCE 24's Selina Sykes reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>'A lot of Ukrainians are feeling extremely betrayed' by Trump's Russian diesel deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:971d3b59c361743064620650f1720531d079b9fbb715ad430564e74718bba331</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T19:04:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/a-lot-of-ukrainians-are-feeling-extremely-betrayed-by-trump-s-russian-diesel-deal--24d304591547.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/a-lot-of-ukrainians-are-feeling-extremely-betrayed-by-trump-s-russian-diesel-deal" /><summary type="html">Reporting from central Ukraine, FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg says that "a lot of Ukrainians are feeling extremely betrayed by a country that until recently they saw not only as an ally but as a beacon of freedom and democracy, a country whose values they should aspire to. All of that is falling apart very quickly and Ukrainians' admiration for the United States is disintegrating."</summary></entry><entry><title>How has the European Union’s major recovery plan benefited the 27 member states?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b47314fcf8147aa61b74c335f8185b0d75573b2f53499778a0f85d14186ae417</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T14:19:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-how-has-the-more-than-_600-billion-recovery-plan-revitalised-europe--6b8c747aa05e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-how-has-the-more-than-%E2%82%AC600-billion-recovery-plan-revitalised-europe" /><summary type="html">The 27 member states of the European Union agreed in July 2020 on a €750 billion post-Covid recovery plan called NextGenerationEU. Its main instrument is the Recovery and Resilience Facility, through which the European Commission has already disbursed €450 billion out of €573 billion. The programme is due to come to an end in a few months. The Commission is currently assessing Member States’ claims for the remaining funds.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU warns online platforms over livestreaming US execution planned by Pentagon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc16ba010812a171d5c6a4bf3fb8ebd79ca2dd3f718136e148f64c3d13c8ce70</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T14:05:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-eu-warns-online-platforms-over-livestreaming-us-execution-planned-by-pentagon--559bc068ffcd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-eu-warns-online-platforms-over-livestreaming-us-execution-planned-by-pentagon" /><summary type="html">The European Union warned digital platforms on Monday against livestreaming the execution of Nidal Hasan, a former US Army psychiatrist who is scheduled to be executed by firing squad on December 3 for killing 13 people at a military base in 2009. Under EU rules, platforms have an obligation to moderate shocking and violent content, including capital punishment.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>NATO's top US commander warns Russia that any 'foolish' attack on allies would be 'futile'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ab71a5f04ce7cfe18654aeaae60d2793b0bacc1a34b93c8bfa5a4673e2fd830a</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T12:41:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-nato-s-top-us-commander-warns-russia-that-any-foolish-attack-on-allies-would-be-futile--6a6b5384d4d3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-nato-s-top-us-commander-warns-russia-that-any-foolish-attack-on-allies-would-be-futile" /><summary type="html">NATO's top US military commander in Europe said Monday that any "foolish" attack on the alliance would be "utterly futile", a warning to Russia as European fears grow over the threat from Moscow that includes "hybrid" warfare and cyberattacks.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: NATO's top military commander warns Russia over alleged sabotage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a14e59d256d79abc5a9dd165e690992638933f2b69b677f565465cfe12936264</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T12:26:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/replay-nato-s-top-military-commander-warns-russia-over-alleged-sabotage--36373f6834b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/replay-nato-s-top-military-commander-warns-russia-over-alleged-sabotage" /><summary type="html">And as the war in Ukraine continues, Western concerns are growing over Moscow’s alleged campaign of sabotage and interference against Kiev's wartime backers. NATO's top military commander gave a press conference this Monday from Warsaw. US General Alexus Grynkewich looks set to warn Russia over the alliance’s ability to counter-attack. Analysis by FRANCE 24 International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Zelensky says learned of Trump's 'energy ceasefire' through media</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e0663dfe5c3f6f3e6527da3897df5ae9c36e8a090da593f1f41b55b51b92083</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T12:24:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ukraine-zelensky-says-learned-of-trump-s-energy-ceasefire-through-media--eb569c8092c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-zelensky-says-learned-of-trump-s-energy-ceasefire-through-media" /><summary type="html">An Axios report is citing an unnamed US source who says that Donald Trump's surprise energy ceasefire between Russia and Ukraine only concerns oil refineries. Elitsa Gadeva explains what this would mean for both sides.</summary></entry><entry><title>Prison 'Games of Hope' olympics in Italy unite inmates and staff</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f592bf745f449b48fa68fd722d0bcb5db65f2f9c35f430159d09859d12afc85f</id><updated>2026-10-14T13:51:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-12T10:54:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/prison-games-of-hope-olympics-in-italy-unite-inmates-and-staff--1ade90bb6eaa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/prison-games-of-hope-olympics-in-italy-unite-inmates-and-staff" /><summary type="html">Sport has the power to unite, and overcome barriers... In Rome, inmates and prison officers became athletes for the day, and took part in a sort of mini prison olympics. Organised by the John Paul II foundation for sport, this is the third edition of the “Games of Hope”, over a year after it was held in the men's wing of the prison in 2025. Story by Emily Boyle.</summary></entry></feed>
